                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "df101779-11d1-31be-9be1-85bc3c2a61a6",
                        "entry_id": "2207ab8b-f739-3c75-8cf2-a865279f581b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Angst vor oder auch vehemente Ablehnung von Transsexuellen, Transsexualität"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b1c9f35-5bee-43d4-a1f3-c1fe936baf0f",
                                "sense_id": "df101779-11d1-31be-9be1-85bc3c2a61a6",
                                "text": "„Zum weltweiten Aktionstag gegen Homophobie, Transphobie und Biphobie zeigen Politiker und Aktivisten auch in Berlin und Brandenburg Flagge.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "92f64998-f853-428e-899f-4773afde8d2f",
                        "source_entry_id": "2207ab8b-f739-3c75-8cf2-a865279f581b",
                        "source_sense_id": "df101779-11d1-31be-9be1-85bc3c2a61a6",
                        "source_sense_description": "Angst vor oder auch vehemente Ablehnung von Transsexuellen, Transsexualität",
                        "target_lang_word": "transphobia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "transphobia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd7247e0-6fd2-3449-bb3d-f0f66f6311d1",
                                        "entry_id": "84ac2ba0-b3bd-3378-a3a6-bf5174e55c59",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Hatred or fear of, or prejudice against, transgender and transsexual people."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bb858c4-fa9a-41e5-890e-c5d0420a2162",
                                                "sense_id": "fd7247e0-6fd2-3449-bb3d-f0f66f6311d1",
                                                "text": "It is not really a debate about privacy and personal safety versus politics, so much as an impulse towards pride and a rejection of internalized transphobia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "418557e3-bb9e-4da5-872b-af1c0485420c",
                                                "sense_id": "fd7247e0-6fd2-3449-bb3d-f0f66f6311d1",
                                                "text": "In this case, transphobia is represented in Pollock's terms as both the \"condition and the effect\" of Cameron's social existence."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bf4d39d4-1922-3fd4-bcef-60d11145036c",
                                        "entry_id": "84ac2ba0-b3bd-3378-a3a6-bf5174e55c59",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The preference of pairs of high-trans effect soft ligands to avoid being mutually trans by becoming cis and having other low-trans effect hard ligands trans to themselves."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da0ededb-4538-4545-a61c-508780a90132",
                                                "sense_id": "bf4d39d4-1922-3fd4-bcef-60d11145036c",
                                                "text": "This unusual reactivity and the selectivity observed can be explained as a consequence of the high transphobia of aryl and P-donor ligands […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0183b877-0859-4453-a14d-7731fadf7b4b",
                                                "sense_id": "bf4d39d4-1922-3fd4-bcef-60d11145036c",
                                                "text": "The reactions of trans-[Pt(Mef)Br(PPh₃)₂] with AgBF₄ and Ph₃ECHC(O)R (E = P, R = Me, OMe, Ph; E = As, R = Me) afford only trans-[Pt(Mef){OC(=CHEPh₃)R}(PPh₃)₂] because the C-alkyl/C-ylide transphobia is greater than the C-alkyl/O-ylide transphobia and also because of the lower steric requirement of the O-ylide ligand."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f3e9240-a7d9-4a4d-bc8d-7f3085bc82c2",
                                                "sense_id": "bf4d39d4-1922-3fd4-bcef-60d11145036c",
                                                "text": "In the symbiotic effect, a hard ligand tends to form ionic M-L bonds in which L retains more negative charge than in a soft ligand case, letting the metal ion keep more of its positive charge and hence attract additional hard ligands, […]. The antisymbiotic effect, also called transphobia, applies to pairs of high trans effect, soft ligands on a soft metal. Where a choice exists, there is a strong tendency for such ligands to avoid being mutually trans by becoming cis and preferring to have low trans effect, hard ligands trans to themselves."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
